{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851034-how-can-a-pack-sept-raise-a-caerns-level","id":851034,"title":"How can a pack/sept raise a caerns level?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-22T02:31:34-07:00","id":851034,"title":"How can a pack/sept raise a caerns level?","content":"Is there a possibility that i did not find in W20 to raise the caerns level? For example in Baden-W\u00fcrtemberg (the state in Germany where the Black forrest is), has now the green party in power for one period but will continue to be in power. One of their achievements is the so called black forrest national park which is to the north of the caern of the Get, but even the electorial district where the caern is went green now (first time since WWII that it did not went conservative). <br /> <br /> One thing though, german conservatives are not US ones and there will be a coalition between the greens and the conervatives for the government of the state, but i feel that there would be a great story to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T02:45:45-07:00","id":851036,"title":"","content":"Local human politics aside it's about the power of the totem the resides in the caern. The more garou that are there to support the totem and do deeds in its name will increase the power level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T05:58:43-07:00","id":851100,"title":"","content":"I disagree. Before W20 Rage Across the world, a caern spirit wasn't used similar to a totem anyways.<br /> The Rite of Gathering requires to spend Gnosis to keep the caern alive, it is a fair assumption, that overcharging the Rite could lead to a temporarily excess of spiritual energy in the caern. Meaning, if 5 Gnosis per caern level need to be spend each gathering (monthly) to keep the caern at it's level, then more than that might strengthen the caern, just as to few makes the caern weaker.<br /> <br /> But, if one wants to do more, than a simple numbers game, then geomancy might do the trick. Sure, within the rules only the Stagazers, and the pre-KotE Gaki, had actual rules about gemantic practices, but on the other hand, Fianna are supposed to be in tune with the land and theurges should also have a knack for spirits and spiritual energies - so, from a storytelling standpoint, they would use rites to appeal to the spirits, strengthen them and work on all the caerns typical 'landmarks' like gathering area, shrine for totems, shrines for fallen heroes, housing area and so on. Investing emotional energy as well as actual effort in a meaningful way probably also is a way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T06:42:42-07:00","id":851108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851034-how-can-a-pack-sept-raise-a-caerns-level?p=851100#post851100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Before W20 Rage Across the world, a caern spirit wasn't used similar to a totem anyways.<br /> The Rite of Gathering requires to spend Gnosis to keep the caern alive, it is a fair assumption, that overcharging the Rite could lead to a temporarily excess of spiritual energy in the caern. Meaning, if 5 Gnosis per caern level need to be spend each gathering (monthly) to keep the caern at it's level, then more than that might strengthen the caern, just as to few makes the caern weaker.<br /> <br /> But, if one wants to do more, than a simple numbers game, then geomancy might do the trick. Sure, within the rules only the Stagazers, and the pre-KotE Gaki, had actual rules about gemantic practices, but on the other hand, Fianna are supposed to be in tune with the land and theurges should also have a knack for spirits and spiritual energies - so, from a storytelling standpoint, they would use rites to appeal to the spirits, strengthen them and work on all the caerns typical 'landmarks' like gathering area, shrine for totems, shrines for fallen heroes, housing area and so on. Investing emotional energy as well as actual effort in a meaningful way probably also is a way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>KotE has quite a few geomancy Disciplines. They're in the Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T20:56:29-07:00","id":852785,"title":"","content":"The game never had rules that explained mechanically how a Caern's rank could increase or decrease. Yet, there seemed to be an assumption that caerns could increase or decrease in rank. It also seemed to me that the actual rank of a caern was based on external factors that could not be controlled (but perhaps influenced).<br /> <br /> I'll use urban caerns as an example because I think it is easier to understand. Let's say long ago the Glass Walkers (and yes, I know they weren't called Glass Walkers back then) performed the Rite of Caern building in London, say during the Anglo-Saxon period. At the time, London wasn't very important, but a low ranking Caern of Plenty was created - let's say Rank 1. As London grew stronger and wealthier, the potential rank increased from 1 to 2. No matter what the Glass Walkers did beforehand, the rank could not increase. London simply wasn't a big enough source of plenty. But once it achieved a certain status and retained it, at that point the local sept could somehow &quot;increase&quot; the rank to 2 (by means never explained). But they couldn't increase it to 3 because London did not embody the concept/trait of &quot;plenty&quot; that well enough. Of course, London eventually became the financial center for the world (and still today is one of the largest). I would expect any Caern of Plenty in London today to be Rank 5. So the Garou somehow improved it - but only when it achieved that in &quot;potential&quot;.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if there is a caern in the countryside that draws strength from a pristine wilderness, and over time that wilderness is visited by more and more people, and villages become towns, and eventually lumberjacks cut down the forest and put up parking lots and an Ikea store, that caern's rank will decrease - no matter what the Garou do during their moots.<br /> <br /> There is a reason the mechanics behind this were never given - this is not something that can be done willy nilly. It can only be done if the ST decides it can be done. But let's say you want to use this as a plot in your game. You've decided the local caern could potentially increase to the next rank. What do you have your players do? These are my thoughts.<br /> <br /> 1) Garou have to figure out that the &quot;potential&quot; rank is now at a new level. This is probably done by high Gnosis characters who spend a lot of time in the Umbra and are sensitive to these things.<br /> <br /> 2) The Garou have to perform some kind of rite involving lots of Gnosis donations and appropriate sacrifices. This would be similar as to the Rite of Caern Building, but different flavor text and mechanics. Adventures might include performing spirit quests to determine the tasks, chiminage, correspondences needed to strengthen the Caern Totem so that it can bind itself deeper with Gaia. Utilize kinfolk to affect human politics and development. And of course, recruit enough other Garou to donate all that Gnosis and defend the caern. This is the meat of the adventure, and the details really depend on the specifics of the caern, its location, why it can improve, etc.<br /> <br /> 3) Last are the actual mechanics (die rolling), assuming you want a real chance of failure.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would increase a Caern Rank simply because more people are voting Green, or that a national park has been established. I would look at real &quot;improvements&quot; (from a Garou's perspective) to see if a rank increase is justified. Has the forest actually grown in size? Are there now bits completely not accessible to the general population? Have extirpated species been successfully reintroduced? Are there noticeable decreases/elimination of kinds of pollution/toxins from the ecosystem? What about the effects on the local human population (and has it decreased to a level where Gaian energy has reclaimed a lot of areas)? Furthermore, have these improvements all together truly justified such a substantial increase in the caern's power (going from Caern 1 to Caern 2 may not seem much, but it is effectively doubling in power. Caerns at higher level already imply a lot of spiritual energy going on, so going from Rank 3 to 4 is a huge move)?<br /> <br /> But, hey, that is up to the ST. Personally, I'd argue that in Werewolf terms, the fall of Detroit and nature reclaiming major parts of the city abandoned by humans is probably generating more potential for caern building or growth, then the local elections of a growing and prosperous industrialized community. I also think it is much easier to arrest a DECLINE in a caern ranking, then it is to increase one (especially a natural caern, as opposed to those weird urban caerns of Weaver nature).<br /> <br /> But if you think there is a good story in it for your chronicle, go for it. Just remember this should be a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T05:46:31-07:00","id":852910,"title":"","content":"Oh i will certainly make it a big deal. Thanks for all the help guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}